            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all six changed paths. The new exempt verb in engine/cmd/review.go only wires CLI parsing to the review/app Exempt use case; the rules (risk grammar, report check, numbered no-overwrite storage) live outside this candidate and are not visible, so they could not be assessed here.",
              "Revisions are validated through the existing bind path, and engine/cmd/review_exempt_test.go covers option-like revisions being refused without writing a file, as well as refusal of declared risk items and of unclear reports with nothing stored.",
              "The report is read from stdin only, and --risk is accepted only by the exempt verb. The refactor of parentFills preserves the previous record and verify output.",
              "No secrets, unsafe input handling, or dependency changes appear in the candidate. The exemption is a declared-risk gate by design, and the usage text states the engine does not compute the risk from the diff, which is the requested behavior rather than a defect introduced here."
            ]
          }
        }
