            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The new exempt verb in engine/cmd/review.go reads the report only from stdin and requires --feature, --base, --head and --risk. It maps a refused report to exit 2 and every other failure to exit 1, and writes nothing on those paths. The tests in engine/cmd/review_exempt_test.go assert each of these outcomes, including that no results directory is created.",
              "The refactor that extracts parentFills keeps the existing sentence for the record and verify verbs. TestRecordAndVerifySayWhatTheParentOfTheChainStillFillsAsBefore asserts the old wording for both, so the existing output is covered against regression.",
              "I checked each phrase asserted by TestUsageDocumentsReviewExempt against the engine usage text in engine/cmd/usage.go and the wrapper text in bin/lib/usage.sh after whitespace normalisation. All of them are present, so that doc-parity test should pass.",
              "The updated verb-list messages in engine/cmd/review.go match the expectations in engine/cmd/review_test.go, engine/cmd/dispatch_routes_test.go and the new exempt tests.",
              "The failure path where the skeleton cannot be written to stdout is covered. It exits 1, names the stored path, and leaves the stored file in place.",
              "I did not check the Exempt service, DecodeExemption, CheckReport and the review check behaviour for exemptions. They are outside this candidate's patch, and the test file refers to review_exempt_check_test.go, which is also not part of it."
            ]
          }
        }
